{
 "_doc": "THE FUTURES AND PRICE BOARDS of Capital-Stack-FinTerminal (#1539): HG (the futures board by asset class, term structure, hedge calculator), EQ > Exchange rates and EQ > Commodity prices. Real delayed quotes only: one free source (`source`, delayed, no key); a row whose contract has no free source (symbol null) shows 'n/a (no free source)', and so does every figure the source does not carry (bid/ask, open interest, settlement). Contract specs are declared here: multiplier (USD per price point; for an FX future the contract size in `size_unit`), tick, months, how many expiries are listed, and the expiry rule (a weekday calendar: exchange holidays are not applied, so an expiry can be a day off). A contract symbol is root + month code + two-digit year + '.' + suffix; `front` is the source's continuous front-month symbol. Both the commodity prices and the HG energy / metals / agriculture rows read the same front symbols, so the numbers match across pages; the FX table and the hedge calculator read the same spot symbols. scripts/gen-quotes-snapshot.py bakes data/quotes-snapshot.json; the app refreshes the page on open or pull (no polling) from the same source.",
 "source": {
  "id": "yahoo_chart",
  "label": "Yahoo Finance chart API (delayed quotes)",
  "url": "https://query1.finance.yahoo.com/v8/finance/chart/{symbol}?range=1y&interval=1d",
  "delay": "delayed 15 min (exchange delay)",
  "user_agent": "Mozilla/5.0"
 },
